.TH KLICKY 1 "October 2026" "Klicky 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
klicky \- low-latency mechanical keyboard sounds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B klicky
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Klicky is a small daemon that plays mechanical keyboard sounds for global keypresses.
On Linux it reads keyboard events through evdev and works independently of Wayland or X11.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start the daemon in the foreground.
Startup is exclusive: another instance cannot take ownership while the daemon
is starting or stopping. Failed initialization releases ownership and cleans up.
.TP
.B start --benchmark
Start the daemon and print mapped key names with input-to-dispatch timing.
Do not use benchmark mode while entering sensitive information.
.TP
.B stop
Stop a running daemon through its Unix socket.
Wait up to three seconds for shutdown to be confirmed. Sending the request alone
does not count as success. A missing socket, IPC failure, or a process that does
not exit produces an error (nonzero exit status) unless termination is confirmed.
Stopping an already stopped daemon succeeds.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon state, selected sound pack, and volume.
The running and responsive fields are yes only when an event-loop IPC reply
matches the recorded live PID. The process exists field separately reports PID
liveness. A live but unresponsive process is not reported as a running daemon.
Responsiveness does not test keyboard input or audio playback.
.TP
.B list
List user and system sound packs.
.TP
.BI switch " NAME"
Select a sound pack immediately, or save it for the next start when the daemon is stopped.
.TP
.BI volume " LEVEL"
Set playback volume between 0.0 and 1.0.
.TP
.BI service " enable|disable|start|stop|status"
Manage automatic startup and the background user service. Enable starts Klicky now
and at future logins. Start and stop only affect the current session.
Start and enable wait up to three seconds after the service manager returns for
the daemon event loop to respond. A timeout does not undo the service-manager
action: inspect service status before retrying.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the Klicky version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/klicky/config.toml
Per-user configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/klicky/sounds/
Per-user sound packs. These override system packs with the same name.
.TP
.I /usr/share/klicky/sounds/
Package-managed system sound packs.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/klicky/
Owner-only PID file, Unix socket, and persistent klicky.lock file.
Only the daemon holding the lock removes PID/socket state. The stop client never
unlinks these files. After a crash or forced termination, the next startup
reclaims stale state under the lock. Do not delete runtime files while Klicky is
active, and do not unlink the lock file between starts.
.SH SERVICE
Linux uses a systemd user unit. macOS uses a per-user LaunchAgent.
Enable automatic startup for the current user with:
.PP
.nf
klicky service enable
.fi
.PP
Use the service manager to inspect or stop an unresponsive service. Linux systemd
retains its configured stop timeout and termination policy. macOS service stop
uses the same acknowledged stop operation as the direct command; it does not
force-kill a hung daemon. On macOS, disable also requires confirmed shutdown
before removing login configuration. Lifecycle acknowledgments require a daemon built with
the same protocol; stop an older installed daemon before replacing its binary.
.PP
On macOS, start and enable require a regular executable at ~/.local/bin/klicky.
They never register the invoking executable's build path. Symlinked binaries or
redirected installation directories are rejected. Run ./scripts/install-macos.sh
from the repository to install or repair this path. Start and enable update older
daemon property lists to the validated path and current recovery policy.
.PP
The macOS daemon LaunchAgent uses KeepAlive with SuccessfulExit=false and a
30-second ThrottleInterval. Unsuccessful exits are retried; a successful
acknowledged stop exits with status zero. Repeated startup failures may continue
retrying at the throttled rate until stopped; this is not a retry-count limit.
Direct stop and service stop unload the job after confirmed shutdown to cancel
pending retries while retaining the login property list. Disable also removes
the login configuration. A readiness timeout does not cancel a queued retry.
This policy requires validation with a real launchd session in addition to unit tests.
.PP
With a running daemon, sound-control commands report delivery rather than confirmed
pack loading or configuration persistence. Inspect daemon output or service logs
if a switch fails or a setting does not survive restart.
.SH SECURITY
Klicky receives raw global key-down events, including events generated while entering sensitive text.
Normal mode does not store, transmit, or log typed input.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR udev (7)
